# Analyze > CFD table end to end: choosing the method starts a real solve (the example's ten Mach numbers on the GPU), the script
# waits for it (the headless driver runs every task to its end before the next step, so the solve is finished when the
# screenshot is taken: about 5 to 6 minutes on an Apple M1 Max, see the notes in cfd.rs), then the plots show the table.
#   cargo run -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/cfd-solve.drive out/cfd-solve
viewport 1300x800
click "Analyze"
click "CFD table"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot solved-dark.png
click "Light"
move (100, 700)
move (102, 702)
screenshot solved-light.png
click "Dark"
# The geometry did not change: the table stays fresh. Compare with Extended.
click "Compare ▾"
click "Compare with Extended"
move (700, 300)
move (702, 302)
screenshot vs-extended-dark.png
